(GRM-05: append_stmt's first form - "append" expr "to" name "." - a
 single value onto a buffer/list. The second form ("append each name from
 expr to name (treating expr as expr)? .") is GRM-16's row: it parses
 differently from how this production literally states it, and its
 `treating` clause is a silent no-op - see Discrepancy 3. Cross-ref BUF-31
 (buffers.md) for the buffer-append semantics this exercises.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox GRM-05.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   hi there
)
a buffer called greeting is 32 bytes in size.
append "hi" to greeting.
append " there" to greeting.
Print greeting.
